WEBVTT

00:00.363 --> 00:03.227
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.817 --> 00:07.081
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.117 --> 00:10.648
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.683 --> 00:13.648
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.683 --> 00:17.146
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.182 --> 00:20.412
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.447 --> 00:22.013
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.048 --> 00:23.379
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.413 --> 00:23.850
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.041 --> 00:36.672
<i>We now return
to the All in the Family</i>

00:36.708 --> 00:38.838
<i>and Modern Family
crossover episode.</i>

00:38.874 --> 00:40.038
Hello,
Mr. Bunker.

00:40.074 --> 00:41.371
We brought
some hummus.

00:41.407 --> 00:43.371
Oh, yeah, I knew
them two was hummus

00:43.407 --> 00:45.171
the minute
they walked in the door.

00:45.206 --> 00:49.003
Yay! A crossover always brings
out the best in each show!

00:49.038 --> 00:51.403
It certainly doesn't smack
of desperation.

00:51.438 --> 00:53.503
The priorities
are always creative,

00:53.538 --> 00:55.036
and not driven
by marketing or...

00:55.071 --> 00:56.502
Okay, that's
enough.

00:56.537 --> 00:58.468
Oh, my God!
What is it, Peter?

00:58.504 --> 01:00.901
Look at this. Dennis the Menace
is just shoveling snow.

01:00.936 --> 01:02.502
He's being helpful.

01:02.537 --> 01:04.367
<i>Might as well just
call it Dennis now.</i>

01:04.403 --> 01:05.968
He's not a menace.

01:06.002 --> 01:07.834
Not every strip
is gonna be hilarious.

01:07.870 --> 01:10.300
You know something? I could
do better than these idiots.

01:10.336 --> 01:12.566
I should just go down to
the paper and sell 'em my own.

01:12.602 --> 01:14.799
Well, Peter, you might be
underestimating the difficulty

01:14.801 --> 01:16.365
of writing a comic strip.

01:16.401 --> 01:18.931
As someone who occasionally
dates the creative muse,

01:18.967 --> 01:22.197
I can vouch for the unforgiving
face of a blank sheet of paper.

01:22.233 --> 01:24.730
In fact, I think it was
William Faulkner who said...

01:24.766 --> 01:26.997
I'm back. I'm published.
Check it out.

01:30.465 --> 01:32.596
<i>I call my comic
For Pete's Sake,</i>

01:32.631 --> 01:34.063
because it points out things

01:34.098 --> 01:36.928
that make you shake your head
and say, "For Pete's sake."

01:36.964 --> 01:38.429
This one's for tomorrow.

01:42.463 --> 01:43.661
These are
good, Peter.

01:43.697 --> 01:45.594
I like how
you retell tired old gags

01:45.629 --> 01:47.660
with a detached,
ironic approach.

01:47.696 --> 01:49.527
Yeah, plus,
it's all brand-new jokes

01:49.562 --> 01:51.093
that I'm really,
really serious about.

01:51.129 --> 01:52.459
Well, good for you, Peter,

01:52.495 --> 01:54.426
but how did you get published
so quickly?

01:54.461 --> 01:56.793
Ah, the editor of the paper
owed me a favor.

01:56.828 --> 01:58.458
I got him a picture
of Spider-Man.

01:58.494 --> 02:01.125
Why can't anyone get me
a picture of the Spider-Man?!

02:01.160 --> 02:02.791
Here you go.

02:05.426 --> 02:08.957
Yeah, I got a whole subreddit
of superhero thong shots.

02:12.126 --> 02:14.323
Here's your beer, Peter.

02:14.358 --> 02:15.756
Thanks, Jerome.
What do I owe you?

02:15.791 --> 02:18.255
Nah, you already
paid me... in laughs.

02:23.256 --> 02:24.788
I do a lot of island ones.

02:24.823 --> 02:26.054
Peter, you
should do one

02:26.089 --> 02:28.121
where a baseball player
can't steal second,

02:28.156 --> 02:29.854
'cause he's
on probation.

02:29.889 --> 02:31.453
For drug crimes.

02:31.489 --> 02:32.754
Political.

02:32.789 --> 02:34.452
Yeah, you put an island
in there, you're in business.

02:34.488 --> 02:36.219
Hey, how about one
where you draw a sock,

02:36.254 --> 02:37.719
and it says "Sock it to me,"

02:37.755 --> 02:40.085
or-or maybe draw Lois
taking a hot-tub dump,

02:40.121 --> 02:41.951
and she just says whatever?

02:47.853 --> 02:49.850
Peter, your comic
in this morning's paper

02:49.885 --> 02:51.649
is really offensive.

02:56.318 --> 02:57.949
That's not funny, Peter.

02:57.984 --> 02:59.615
Ah, you're just not
getting it, Lois.

02:59.650 --> 03:01.548
See, his wife washed
dishes for him.

03:01.584 --> 03:03.081
Oh, for Pete's sake.

03:03.117 --> 03:05.614
Aha! There you go.

03:05.649 --> 03:06.881
Peter, you should see this.

03:06.916 --> 03:08.214
Your dishwasher cartoon

03:08.249 --> 03:09.880
has really outraged
the online community.

03:09.915 --> 03:11.147
What?

03:11.182 --> 03:12.546
Gosh, it's not
like the Internet

03:12.582 --> 03:14.613
to go crazy about something
small and stupid.

03:14.648 --> 03:15.979
Peter, you have
to apologize.

03:16.014 --> 03:17.278
What, because of a joke?

03:17.314 --> 03:18.512
Not just a joke, Peter.

03:18.547 --> 03:20.778
A joke that angered some bloggers.

03:20.813 --> 03:22.278
Well, I guess this
ain't the first time

03:22.314 --> 03:24.378
I got in trouble for something
I said about a woman.

03:25.912 --> 03:28.211
Oh, good.
We can steal.

03:34.145 --> 03:35.942
<i>And welcome back
to The Flow.</i>

03:35.977 --> 03:37.210
We're talking
to Peter Griffin,

03:37.244 --> 03:39.209
<i>the artist behind
For Pete's Sake,</i>

03:39.244 --> 03:42.042
which has caused outrage
with a misogynistic comic.

03:42.077 --> 03:43.575
Here's a video
of some outrage.

03:47.510 --> 03:49.407
Boo!

03:49.442 --> 03:51.207
Yeah, those boos
don't hurt so much

03:51.242 --> 03:53.473
'cause you spent two minutes
of the last segment

03:53.508 --> 03:55.240
applauding a red velvet cake.

03:55.274 --> 03:56.705
Ah!

03:58.974 --> 04:00.373
And if that's not bad enough,

04:00.407 --> 04:01.971
this morning's cartoon
is even worse.

04:02.006 --> 04:03.405
Let's put that up.

04:09.405 --> 04:11.204
Mr. Griffin,
do you really think

04:11.239 --> 04:12.903
this is an
appropriate cartoon

04:12.939 --> 04:14.736
to run on Gloria Steinem's
half-birthday?

04:14.771 --> 04:15.902
You sound angry.

04:15.938 --> 04:17.535
Did one of your
friends get engaged?

04:17.571 --> 04:20.369
You have no idea how offensive
you are to women, do you?

04:20.404 --> 04:21.569
What?! I love women.

04:21.604 --> 04:23.801
I bet I can name more
porn stars than you.

04:23.837 --> 04:26.102
But-but don't tell my wife
how many porn stars I know.

04:26.136 --> 04:27.533
I'll get in a
lot of trouble.

04:27.569 --> 04:28.800
I know all of
'em, though.

04:28.836 --> 04:29.967
There are people

04:30.001 --> 04:31.633
who just started an hour
ago, and I know 'em.

04:34.668 --> 04:36.400
Your cartoon is sexist!

04:36.434 --> 04:38.032
Down with misogyny!

04:38.067 --> 04:41.765
It wasn't even funny, and
I have a great sense of humor.

04:41.800 --> 04:44.032
Man, they seem really upset.

04:44.067 --> 04:45.864
I was just trying
to make people laugh.

04:45.899 --> 04:47.731
Dad, I'm worried
they're gonna hurt us.

04:47.766 --> 04:49.098
No, no,
they're angry, Chris,

04:49.133 --> 04:51.097
but they ain't
gonna get violent.

04:51.132 --> 04:53.429
Oh, cool!
That brick I ordered.

04:53.465 --> 04:55.496
<i>Wait a minute.
I didn't order this brick.</i>

04:55.531 --> 04:56.730
You may be right, Chris.

04:56.765 --> 04:58.296
Peter, this is
getting out of hand.

04:58.330 --> 04:59.962
I don't feel safe
in my own home.

04:59.997 --> 05:02.261
Maybe we should get out
of Quahog for a while.

05:02.297 --> 05:03.594
You know, she's right.

05:03.629 --> 05:05.295
We should get out of town
till this all blows over.

05:05.330 --> 05:07.394
Okay, we'll go,
but just give me a minute.

05:07.429 --> 05:09.761
<i>I just want to turn in
my last For Pete's Sake.</i>

05:12.695 --> 05:16.293
<i>going out on top amid a flurry
of gambling rumors.</i>

05:27.824 --> 05:29.419
Peter, where are we?

05:29.419 --> 05:30.860
I don't know.
I just woke up, too.

05:30.861 --> 05:32.726
I tied the steering
wheel to my belt.

05:32.760 --> 05:35.558
I figure we've been on the
road about 20% of the time.

05:35.593 --> 05:37.691
Dad, how long
until we can go back home?

05:37.726 --> 05:39.023
Um, I don't know.

05:39.059 --> 05:40.823
How long do women
hold grudges?

05:40.858 --> 05:42.389
Not very long,
I'm guessing.

05:42.425 --> 05:44.356
Oh, Peter, we've been
driving all night.

05:44.391 --> 05:45.989
Pull over
to that gas station.

05:46.024 --> 05:48.122
We can use the bathroom
and stretch our legs.

05:48.158 --> 05:49.322
You got it, babe.

05:49.357 --> 05:50.789
Did you call me "babe"?

05:50.824 --> 05:51.622
I did.

05:51.657 --> 05:53.455
Oh, Peter.

05:54.956 --> 05:56.554
Ew! Mom!

05:56.589 --> 05:59.321
You'll never
have this, Meg.

06:02.155 --> 06:03.787
All right, back
in the car, kids.

06:03.822 --> 06:05.886
For this leg of the
trip, I was thinking

06:05.921 --> 06:08.319
of driving with my shirt
off like New Mexico trash.

06:11.554 --> 06:13.484
Oh, my God!
Our car!

06:13.520 --> 06:14.884
Someone's stealing it.

06:14.919 --> 06:16.084
Ah, crap.

06:16.119 --> 06:17.284
Although, I got to say,

06:17.320 --> 06:19.617
you never get to see
somebody else driving your car.

06:19.652 --> 06:21.250
It's kind of cool.
Kind of weird.

06:21.285 --> 06:22.483
We're stuck
here, Peter!

06:22.519 --> 06:24.216
And we don't even
know where we are.

06:24.252 --> 06:26.582
Well, there's a sign.

06:43.315 --> 06:45.413
Huh, guess we're in a town
called Springfield.

06:45.448 --> 06:47.413
Springfield, eh?
What state?

06:47.448 --> 06:49.612
I can't imagine
we're allowed to say.

07:13.277 --> 07:15.107
Well, this Springfield place
seems nice.

07:15.143 --> 07:16.474
We should visit here again.

07:16.510 --> 07:18.874
I don't know, Lois. This
seems like a one-shot deal.

07:18.909 --> 07:20.740
Guys, we ain't here
for fun, all right?

07:20.776 --> 07:23.073
We're here to find the police,
report our stolen car.

07:23.108 --> 07:24.506
Oh, and don't
drink the water.

07:24.541 --> 07:26.673
Everybody around here looks
like they have hepatitis.

07:26.708 --> 07:28.239
Dad, I'm
starving.

07:28.274 --> 07:29.605
Can we get
some food?!

07:29.640 --> 07:31.972
Lois, whip out your boob,
give the boy his lunch.

07:32.007 --> 07:33.171
Listen to
the man.

07:33.206 --> 07:34.904
Yeah, Lois,
listen to the man.

07:34.940 --> 07:37.238
How about we just go into
that store there?

07:41.139 --> 07:42.803
Uh, uh, excuse me?

07:42.838 --> 07:45.036
Hello. Welcome
to the Kwik-E-Mart.

07:48.304 --> 07:50.635
Oh, I am so sorry.
Let me unplug that.

07:50.671 --> 07:53.001
Oh, such a nuisance!

07:53.037 --> 07:54.734
Hello, funny-sounding
Cleveland.

07:54.770 --> 07:56.167
What's the specialty
of the house?

07:56.202 --> 07:58.633
To you, I recommend...
the donut.

08:00.936 --> 08:02.301
Ooh!

08:02.336 --> 08:03.666
Yum!

08:03.701 --> 08:05.999
Have you guys seriously
never heard of donuts?

08:06.035 --> 08:07.766
These are made
fresh every day.

08:07.801 --> 08:09.766
And then, several days
later, we receive them

08:09.801 --> 08:11.564
and make them available
for purchase.

08:11.600 --> 08:13.331
Hey, are these...
are these free?

08:13.366 --> 08:16.498
'Cause I forgot to mention, all
our money is in our stolen car.

08:16.532 --> 08:18.031
Thank you. Come again.

08:18.066 --> 08:21.130
Sir, we can pay you back for
the donuts when we find our car.

08:21.165 --> 08:23.696
Do you think that I am moved
by your sob story?

08:23.731 --> 08:25.430
I come from a country
where the words

08:25.465 --> 08:27.296
for "sewage" and "beverage"
are the same.

08:27.331 --> 08:29.129
I'll pay for their donuts.

08:32.931 --> 08:34.761
Thank you so
much, sir.

08:34.796 --> 08:36.428
For what?
I didn't say anything.

08:36.462 --> 08:37.594
Oh.

08:37.629 --> 08:39.460
It was me.

08:42.695 --> 08:45.693
How come this convenience store
has so many shadowy parts?

08:45.728 --> 08:48.959
Apu, a dozen donuts for
our albino visitors.

08:48.994 --> 08:50.425
Wow! For real?!

08:50.460 --> 08:53.425
No man should be so poor
he cannot pay for a donut.

08:53.460 --> 08:54.958
I was once you.

08:54.993 --> 08:56.392
I couldn't afford donuts.

08:56.426 --> 08:58.724
Tell them what I did, Apu.
He stole the donuts.

08:58.760 --> 09:00.456
I stole the donuts.

09:00.492 --> 09:01.823
So, here you go.

09:01.859 --> 09:03.623
12... ten...
eight donuts.

09:03.659 --> 09:05.923
That's very nice
of you, Mister...?

09:05.958 --> 09:07.923
Simpson. Homer Simpson.

09:07.958 --> 09:09.322
We're the Griffins.

09:09.357 --> 09:11.888
Peter, Lois, Stewie, and then,
uh, you know, the others.

09:11.924 --> 09:13.755
Brian, I guess.

09:13.790 --> 09:15.987
Well, enjoy
your... six donuts.

09:17.689 --> 09:20.154
Mmm. Yummy... donut.

09:20.189 --> 09:22.553
That's pretty good,
but try it like this.

09:23.688 --> 09:26.286
Mmm. Donut.

09:27.321 --> 09:30.085
Mmm. Donut.

09:30.121 --> 09:35.018
I think you and I are
gonna get along just okay.

09:39.835 --> 09:41.433
Yeah, all right,
we'll be there.

09:41.467 --> 09:43.832
But if you want
to save us a little time,

09:43.867 --> 09:46.898
you can start
tracing his body with chalk.

09:46.933 --> 09:49.931
This is the
police station.

09:49.966 --> 09:54.363
Be careful. I think some
of them might be cops.

09:54.398 --> 09:56.230
Oh, hey there.
Cool hat, weird nose.

09:56.265 --> 09:57.730
Hey, listen,
my car got stolen.

09:57.765 --> 09:59.096
I was hoping
you could help.

09:59.131 --> 10:00.463
Well, we got
a procedure

10:00.498 --> 10:02.295
for handling alleged
crimes around here.

10:02.330 --> 10:03.995
Let's see. Uh, did
you contribute

10:04.030 --> 10:05.495
to the policeman's ball?

10:05.531 --> 10:06.895
No.

10:06.930 --> 10:09.394
Oh, that's too bad,
'cause he really needs one.

10:09.430 --> 10:11.428
He had an accident last week.

10:11.463 --> 10:14.293
Yeah, I tried to jump
over a parking meter.

10:14.328 --> 10:15.994
Yeah, all right,
well, with no contribution,

10:16.029 --> 10:19.093
your report goes right
into the circular file.

10:19.128 --> 10:20.659
I got to be honest.

10:20.694 --> 10:22.325
I don't usually check this file,

10:22.361 --> 10:25.391
so it might be a while
until we find that car of yours.

10:25.427 --> 10:28.658
Uh, Chief, that excuse to
leave you asked for is here.

10:28.693 --> 10:30.490
Oh, sorry,
I got to take this.

10:30.526 --> 10:32.924
It never ends.

10:36.125 --> 10:37.357
Oh, thank you so much

10:37.392 --> 10:39.489
for putting us up
until we find our car.

10:39.525 --> 10:42.222
And thank you for not being
a band of hippie murderers.

10:42.258 --> 10:43.889
And now
this again.

10:43.924 --> 10:46.355
You bring home two bands
of hippie murderers,

10:46.390 --> 10:48.188
and suddenly,
that's all you're about.

10:48.223 --> 10:50.188
Well, what do you say we have
some lunch?

10:50.223 --> 10:51.521
Where's
Bart?

10:51.556 --> 10:53.154
Well, he's at
camp all week.

10:53.189 --> 10:55.187
I'm sorry you
won't get to meet him.

10:59.121 --> 11:01.153
Got kicked out of camp.

11:01.188 --> 11:04.252
I superglued my counselor's
butt cheeks together.

11:04.287 --> 11:05.519
That's terrible.

11:05.554 --> 11:08.684
But how did you even get access
to his butt cheeks?

11:08.720 --> 11:10.917
I'm not the only one
who got kicked out of camp.

11:10.952 --> 11:12.050
This is Bart.

11:12.086 --> 11:13.451
Honey, your hands
are filthy.

11:13.485 --> 11:14.984
Go wash up
for lunch.

11:15.019 --> 11:16.483
Eat my shorts!

11:16.519 --> 11:17.817
"Eat my shorts."

11:17.852 --> 11:20.150
I love that!
Is that a popular expression,

11:20.185 --> 11:22.616
like "what the deuce"?
Probably more popular.

11:22.651 --> 11:24.748
Probably... probably
way more popular.

11:24.784 --> 11:27.448
Well, here's my room.

11:27.483 --> 11:29.181
Hey, you want to see
my weapons closet?

11:29.216 --> 11:31.481
You have a
weapons closet, too?

11:39.681 --> 11:42.578
Ouch! Jesus
heard my mean thought!

11:42.614 --> 11:44.779
A slingshot!
It's so simple and pure.

11:44.814 --> 11:46.912
He doesn't need lasers
or time machines,

11:46.946 --> 11:49.511
just gum balls and marbles
and balls of string.

11:49.546 --> 11:51.778
He's like something
out of Mark Twain!

11:51.813 --> 11:53.811
Whose real name
was Samuel Clemens.

11:53.846 --> 11:56.010
How... how does that further
this conversation?

11:56.045 --> 11:58.410
Hey, you want to make
a prank phone call?

11:58.445 --> 11:59.942
Ooh, prank phone call!

12:04.811 --> 12:06.509
Moe's Tavern.
Moe speaking.

12:06.544 --> 12:08.207
Uh, yeah, I'm looking
for a friend,

12:08.243 --> 12:10.840
last name Keebum,
first name Lee.

12:10.876 --> 12:12.141
Uh, hang on, I'll check.

12:12.176 --> 12:14.241
Hey, guys, do I got
a Lee Keebum?

12:14.276 --> 12:16.940
Come on, look at the stools--
is there a Lee Keebum?

12:16.976 --> 12:19.773
Somebody check the rear--
I know I got a Lee Keebum.

12:19.808 --> 12:22.006
Then you probably shouldn't
be handling food.

12:25.907 --> 12:27.439
Oh, my God,
that's amazing!

12:27.473 --> 12:29.004
That's the coolest
thing ever!

12:29.039 --> 12:30.871
Hey, I want to try.
Okay.

12:32.773 --> 12:34.437
Moe's Tavern.

12:34.472 --> 12:37.137
Hello, Moe?
Your sister's being raped.

12:37.172 --> 12:39.736
Is that... is that one?

12:39.772 --> 12:41.202
So, this is my room.

12:41.238 --> 12:42.803
Please excuse the mess.

12:42.838 --> 12:45.002
There, that's better.

12:45.037 --> 12:47.001
Look at all these trophies!

12:47.036 --> 12:49.068
There must be,
like, 20 of them!

12:49.103 --> 12:52.401
23. But I'm sure you have
a lot of trophies of your own.

12:52.436 --> 12:54.666
No. I'm not good
at anything.

12:54.702 --> 12:57.566
Oh, Meg, I'm sure
you're good at something.

12:57.602 --> 12:59.566
We just have
to find out what it is.

12:59.602 --> 13:03.032
After all, Nelson Mandela said
it's our obligation to shine.

13:03.068 --> 13:05.365
You mean like my
oily face and back?

13:05.401 --> 13:07.798
No. Maybe don't sit
on my bedspread, please.

13:07.833 --> 13:11.065
But I mean the light within you
that makes you an individual.

13:11.100 --> 13:13.564
Meg, you need to know
that you matter.

13:13.600 --> 13:16.131
Really? No one's ever
told me I mattered before.

13:16.166 --> 13:18.029
<i>That's why you
have to say it.</i>

13:18.065 --> 13:20.396
So say it.
I matter.

13:20.431 --> 13:21.431
Louder!

13:21.432 --> 13:22.696
I matter!

13:22.731 --> 13:25.895
Shut up, Meg! You don't matter!

13:43.294 --> 13:46.091
Hey, couldn't help but notice
there's no seat for me.

13:46.127 --> 13:49.825
Oh. I was under the impression
that you were a dog.

13:49.860 --> 13:51.724
You're right to have
that reaction, Marge.

13:51.760 --> 13:54.624
Why, I just figured,
at home I sit with the family,

13:54.659 --> 13:55.957
so I assumed that...

13:55.992 --> 13:58.057
Have you ever drunk
out of a toilet?

13:58.092 --> 14:00.456
I-I don't see what that has
to do with the discussion.

14:00.492 --> 14:02.289
Dogs eat in the kitchen.

14:02.325 --> 14:04.255
Yeah, dogs eat
in the kitchen.

14:04.290 --> 14:06.921
Y-You know, you're eating
mostly horse hooves

14:06.957 --> 14:08.988
and tallow, right?
You cool with that?

14:09.023 --> 14:11.187
Oh, and the ones that
fall on the floor,

14:11.223 --> 14:12.855
you just eat those
up, too, huh?

14:12.890 --> 14:14.320
Oh, yeah, yeah, you do.

14:14.355 --> 14:16.520
So, is that... is that,
like, your thing?

14:16.555 --> 14:18.886
You eat loud?

14:18.921 --> 14:21.586
I... I'm-I'm sorry,
I don't know what...

14:21.621 --> 14:22.919
That's a gutter language.

14:22.955 --> 14:25.219
Are you making friends
in there, Brian?

14:25.254 --> 14:27.018
Yep, he's a lot
of laughs.

14:27.054 --> 14:29.085
Wow, you work at a
nuclear power plant?

14:29.120 --> 14:30.752
What's that?
I don't know.

14:30.787 --> 14:31.951
Pretty impressive.

14:31.986 --> 14:33.684
I just work
at a brewery.

14:33.719 --> 14:36.350
Oh, my God,
you get to work with beer?!

14:36.386 --> 14:38.783
Wow! What's beer really like?

14:38.818 --> 14:41.050
Eh, he's got a big head.

14:41.085 --> 14:43.949
Hey, you know-- aw, damn it,
I don't have a comic strip anymore.

14:43.984 --> 14:47.415
So, still no word from the
police on your stolen car?

14:47.450 --> 14:49.748
The cops
here are a joke.

14:49.783 --> 14:52.514
I bet you and me can find
your car on our own.

14:52.549 --> 14:53.981
You think so?
Yeah.

14:54.016 --> 14:56.047
'Cause Homer Simpson
and Peter Griffin

14:56.082 --> 14:57.780
are a great team!

14:57.815 --> 15:00.046
A greater team than...

15:00.081 --> 15:02.513
Than...
Uh-huh, keep going.

15:02.548 --> 15:04.579
Than... something else.

15:04.614 --> 15:06.846
Something else?
I... don't know what this is.

15:06.881 --> 15:08.811
O-Okay,
I'll do it.

15:08.847 --> 15:11.444
Homer Simpson and Peter Griffin
are an even greater team

15:11.480 --> 15:12.944
than the Air Force!

15:14.979 --> 15:17.510
Hold steady.
I got him in my sights.

15:22.544 --> 15:24.175
Whoo-hoo!
Yeah-heh-heh!

15:24.211 --> 15:26.441
Yeah, we did it.
What's he doing here?

15:26.477 --> 15:29.241
We got to carry him,
'cause he can't fly on his own.

15:29.276 --> 15:31.508
We let that other guy try,
and look what happened.

15:31.542 --> 15:35.208
No, no, no, no, no, no...!

15:40.042 --> 15:43.106
Wow, they've made a lot
of changes to Quahog!

15:43.141 --> 15:45.206
Chris, we're
in a different town.

15:45.241 --> 15:46.372
Oh...

15:46.407 --> 15:48.638
Is that why there was
blood in my stool?

15:48.674 --> 15:50.772
No. That-that sounds
like a separate issue.

15:50.807 --> 15:52.738
God, I can't believe
I got stuck

15:52.773 --> 15:54.604
taking their stupid dog
for a walk.

15:54.639 --> 15:57.303
Stupid? Well, I don't know,
I think he's kind of fun.

15:57.338 --> 15:59.236
What, are you kidding?
He doesn't do anything.

15:59.271 --> 16:00.937
You know,
it's not his fault, though.

16:00.972 --> 16:02.435
He doesn't know any better.

16:02.471 --> 16:04.535
He's been on a leash
his whole life.

16:04.571 --> 16:06.836
Hey, you know what?
Come here, Santa's Stupid Name.

16:06.871 --> 16:10.401
You're a grown dog--
start acting like one.

16:12.836 --> 16:14.900
Come here, boy.

16:16.269 --> 16:17.800
Hey, stop that dog!

16:19.103 --> 16:21.367
Sorry. We're
on a smoke break.

16:23.768 --> 16:25.932
Nothing beats
smoking and standing.

16:25.967 --> 16:29.531
Although smoking and sitting
does have its moments.

16:29.567 --> 16:32.731
You always have
to argue with me.

16:37.332 --> 16:39.130
Oh, thank goodness!

16:39.165 --> 16:42.696
I was starting to think
you wouldn't show, Dr. Dog.

16:46.964 --> 16:50.628
Boy, you really like
to bleed, huh, guy?

16:57.396 --> 17:00.294
Hey, there's a dog
in the dining area!

17:00.328 --> 17:01.859
How'd that happen?

17:01.894 --> 17:03.726
Get back in there.

17:08.627 --> 17:10.225
Which one is Santa's
Little Helper?

17:10.260 --> 17:12.858
I don't know. You're the one who
sniffed his butt.

17:12.893 --> 17:14.557
Yeah, for, like,
a second!

17:16.859 --> 17:18.191
Damn it, he's gone.

17:18.226 --> 17:19.656
We're screwed.

17:19.691 --> 17:22.522
Welcome to Krusty Burger.
May I take your order?

17:22.558 --> 17:25.255
Your voice
sounds stupid.

17:45.088 --> 17:46.885
Oh, my God,
that was great!

17:46.921 --> 17:49.852
I mean, unless you think it sucked,
in which case it sucked.

17:49.886 --> 17:51.185
It was all right, dude.

17:51.220 --> 17:52.484
Yeah, dude.

17:52.519 --> 17:54.684
So, you know, um,
I'm only wearing this diaper

17:54.720 --> 17:57.484
as a dare, you know-- it's not,
like, an everyday thing.

17:57.519 --> 17:59.883
Hey, loser, I copied
off your spelling test

17:59.919 --> 18:02.183
and got a D!

18:02.218 --> 18:04.083
Haw-haw!

18:04.118 --> 18:07.049
I say, how long has that boy
been treating you like that?

18:07.085 --> 18:11.715
Uh...
about 24 years.

18:13.450 --> 18:14.848
Aah!

18:19.315 --> 18:21.879
Just who I was
looking for!

18:27.581 --> 18:29.845
Cowabunga.

18:33.034 --> 18:35.132
All right, Peter, if we're
gonna find your car,

18:35.168 --> 18:36.766
we got to think
like a car.

18:36.801 --> 18:39.232
So let's fill up
at that gas station.

18:46.699 --> 18:48.664
I feel sick.
Keep drinking.

18:48.699 --> 18:50.497
I prepaid 40 bucks!

18:50.532 --> 18:52.529
Homer, maybe
we're doing this wrong.

18:56.431 --> 18:58.096
Oh, crap.

19:03.263 --> 19:06.295
<i>Haben Sie Homer und
Peter MIT Chevron pump?</i>

19:11.096 --> 19:15.059
Okay, I got a great idea how
we're gonna find my stolen car.

19:15.095 --> 19:18.292
We'll throw a car wash--
free for stolen cars!

19:18.327 --> 19:21.859
And then when we find it,
we'll actually charge the guy!

19:31.659 --> 19:33.423
Well, none of these
is my car,

19:33.459 --> 19:35.723
but we promised
these scumbags a show.

19:51.222 --> 19:54.020
♪ Love is like a bomb, baby,
come on, get it on ♪

19:54.055 --> 19:56.785
♪ Livin' like a lover
with a radar phone ♪

19:56.821 --> 19:58.952
♪ Lookin' like a tramp,
like a video vamp ♪

19:58.988 --> 20:02.418
♪ Demolition woman,
can I be your man? ♪

20:03.720 --> 20:05.352
♪ Yeah! ♪

20:07.386 --> 20:11.217
♪ So come on, take a bottle ♪

20:11.252 --> 20:13.783
♪ Shake it up ♪

20:13.819 --> 20:16.483
♪ Break the bubble ♪

20:16.518 --> 20:19.282
♪ Break it up ♪

20:19.317 --> 20:20.582
♪ Pour some ♪

20:20.617 --> 20:21.848
♪ Sugar on me ♪

20:21.883 --> 20:24.748
♪ Ooh, in the name of love ♪

20:24.783 --> 20:26.448
♪ Pour some ♪

20:26.483 --> 20:28.247
♪ Sugar on me ♪

20:28.283 --> 20:30.014
♪ Come on, fire me up ♪

20:30.049 --> 20:31.747
♪ Pour your ♪

20:31.782 --> 20:34.046
♪ Sugar on me ♪

20:34.082 --> 20:36.313
♪ I can't get enough... ♪

20:36.349 --> 20:39.412
Hey, Chief, we could arrest every single
car thief in Springfield.

20:39.448 --> 20:41.245
After the show, Lou,

20:41.281 --> 20:43.611
after the show.

20:54.412 --> 20:59.142
I don't know!
I feel like I'm good at nothing!

20:59.178 --> 21:01.976
Hey, everyone gets down
on themselves sometimes.

21:02.011 --> 21:05.808
Those are the days
I'm glad I have my saxophone.

21:05.843 --> 21:06.842
Saxophone?

21:06.843 --> 21:08.507
Yeah. My dad
gave it to me.

21:08.543 --> 21:10.707
My dad once gave me
a gun to hide.

21:10.742 --> 21:12.341
That's terrible.

21:12.376 --> 21:14.540
Whenever I feel
any pain or loneliness,

21:14.575 --> 21:17.440
I just play away the blues
on my saxophone.

21:17.475 --> 21:20.039
Huh. I usually
just beat up a cat.

21:21.240 --> 21:24.105
Good thing we don't have a cat.

21:24.140 --> 21:26.770
Why don't you
give it a shot?

22:03.267 --> 22:04.731
Was that good?

22:04.766 --> 22:07.331
It was okay, but it would
be a shame to waste

22:07.366 --> 22:10.863
such great butcher's arms
on a musical instrument.

22:18.364 --> 22:20.629
Wakey, wakey.

22:20.664 --> 22:22.029
Good morning.

22:22.065 --> 22:24.429
You and I have quite a day
ahead of us.

22:35.861 --> 22:39.693
Oh, that's a clown I painted,
so you know I'm truly insane.

22:39.728 --> 22:41.959
You know, Nelson,

22:41.994 --> 22:44.358
I don't doubt that you've
had a twisted childhood.

22:44.393 --> 22:45.758
Most evil people have.

22:45.794 --> 22:48.091
Hitler, Manson, Jaden Smith.

22:48.126 --> 22:50.158
But you're different
from them, aren't you?

22:50.193 --> 22:52.590
Because they're rail-thin,
and you're fat.

22:52.626 --> 22:54.456
You're a little piggy,
aren't you, Nelson?

22:54.491 --> 22:56.456
In fact, I bet
you're hungry right now.

22:56.491 --> 22:58.755
What's that?

22:59.791 --> 23:01.022
I could eat.

23:01.058 --> 23:02.689
Good. Because you're going

23:02.724 --> 23:05.789
to eat... my... shorts.

23:13.489 --> 23:16.120
Homer, you're never going
to believe what we did.

23:16.155 --> 23:18.852
We saw a movie
in the afternoon!

23:18.888 --> 23:20.986
<i>Yeah, we saw
Surf's Up 2.</i>

23:21.021 --> 23:23.652
Marge covered her eyes every
time the penguins surfed.

23:23.688 --> 23:26.785
It made me nervous.
They could drown.

23:26.820 --> 23:29.117
Hey, where's
Santa's Little Helper?

23:29.153 --> 23:31.617
Brian, you took him
for a walk, right?

23:31.652 --> 23:33.583
Uh, yeah, yeah.

23:33.619 --> 23:35.116
More-more like he took me
for a walk.

23:35.152 --> 23:37.317
God, what a...
what a fun dog.

23:37.352 --> 23:40.249
He's in the kitchen right now,
totally accounted for.

23:40.284 --> 23:41.582
Shut up.

23:41.618 --> 23:43.915
I'll, uh... I'll go check
on him right now.

23:43.951 --> 23:45.581
And Chris
will come with me.

23:45.617 --> 23:47.615
But nobody else!

23:50.316 --> 23:51.948
BRIAN
Ruff! Ruff, ruff!

23:51.983 --> 23:53.813
Ah, there he is!

23:53.848 --> 23:56.579
Aw, you like that
behind the ear, don't you, boy?

23:56.615 --> 23:57.713
Ruff! Ruff, ruff!

23:57.748 --> 24:00.845
Ruff, ruff! I'm
another dog in here!

24:00.881 --> 24:02.179
What the hell are you doing?

24:02.214 --> 24:04.245
He's having a
dog playdate.

24:04.280 --> 24:07.644
How does that help us?
We're creating a broad story.

24:07.680 --> 24:10.111
Also, Matthew McConaughey
is in here, too!

24:10.147 --> 24:12.244
"All right, all right, all right."

24:12.279 --> 24:14.710
No, no, he's-he's not
really in here! He's...

24:14.745 --> 24:17.009
We-we thought it was him,
but it was just the oven!

24:17.045 --> 24:18.076
Now you're just doing voices.

24:18.111 --> 24:20.276
Jack Nicholson?!

24:20.312 --> 24:22.809
Okay, Santa's Little Helper
got all tuckered out

24:22.844 --> 24:25.475
from his playdate, so he went
out back to take a nap

24:25.511 --> 24:27.741
under that tree where nobody
knows quite where it is.

24:27.777 --> 24:29.274
Hey, what happened
to Jack Nicholson

24:29.310 --> 24:30.907
and that other dog?
Yep.

24:30.943 --> 24:33.674
Wait, aren't you supposed
to be looking for our car?

24:33.709 --> 24:34.806
Didn't find the car, Lois,

24:34.841 --> 24:36.706
but I found a good
time with a good pal.

24:36.741 --> 24:39.372
Right, Homer? Hey,
Quagmire who, right?

24:39.408 --> 24:41.439
Yeah, Quagmire who?

24:41.474 --> 24:44.571
That's an actual question.
I don't know who Quagmire is.

24:44.607 --> 24:47.971
Peter, I'm glad you made a
friend, but what about our car?

24:48.006 --> 24:49.504
Yeah, I got an idea
about that.

24:49.539 --> 24:52.504
What's the one surefire way
to find a lost car?

24:52.539 --> 24:55.636
Giant magnet?
Giant magnet.

24:56.672 --> 24:57.802
Giant magnet?

25:00.504 --> 25:01.802
Check.

25:01.837 --> 25:03.135
Giant plug?
Check.

25:03.170 --> 25:05.768
Giant curbside outlet?

25:08.870 --> 25:12.434
Oh, things never work
the way they do on the box.

25:15.602 --> 25:17.440
Okay, let's get this garbage
out of the street.

25:20.834 --> 25:25.465
Oh, dear, I was using that car
as pants.

25:25.500 --> 25:27.731
Oh, my God, Dad,
it's our car!

25:27.767 --> 25:31.330
That confused old guy must have
been driving it by mistake.

25:31.365 --> 25:34.263
How many confused old guys
you got in this town?

25:37.032 --> 25:39.329
I'm old, so I'm the victim!

25:43.131 --> 25:45.495
Well, Homer, thanks
for helping me get my car back.

25:45.530 --> 25:48.295
And to show my appreciation, I
got a little something for you.

25:48.330 --> 25:50.627
Here you go.
Pawtucket Patriot Ale.

25:50.663 --> 25:52.627
The best Quahog
has to offer.

25:52.663 --> 25:55.394
Always keep an emergency
six-pack in my trunk.

25:55.429 --> 25:58.326
Oh, that's cool, bringing
outside beer into my bar.

25:58.361 --> 26:00.293
Down the hatch!

26:01.961 --> 26:03.492
That's pretty good, right?

26:04.527 --> 26:06.158
No.

26:06.193 --> 26:08.158
Huh?
It's not good.

26:08.193 --> 26:09.824
This beer tastes exactly
like Duff.

26:09.860 --> 26:11.823
It's just a lousy rip-off.

26:11.859 --> 26:13.890
Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa!
It's not a rip-off of Duff.

26:13.926 --> 26:17.356
It may have been inspired
by Duff, but I-I like to think

26:17.392 --> 26:19.056
it goes in
a different direction.

26:19.091 --> 26:22.222
No, this is just the same
as Duff, but, like, worse.

26:22.257 --> 26:25.222
Hey, come on, now, this is
my favorite beer you're talking about.

26:25.257 --> 26:27.222
Hell, I work for the company.
It's my livelihood.

26:27.256 --> 26:29.887
Oh, yeah? Well, your livelihood
is based on fraud.

26:29.923 --> 26:31.054
Look at this.

26:31.822 --> 26:34.321
Huh?

26:34.355 --> 26:35.653
It is Duff.

26:35.688 --> 26:37.953
Your beer is
in big trouble!

26:37.988 --> 26:39.619
You can't just slap
a new label on something

26:39.655 --> 26:40.753
and call it your own!

26:40.787 --> 26:43.085
Well, maybe Duff should be
in trouble for,

26:43.121 --> 26:45.019
you know,
not being that great.

26:46.387 --> 26:48.717
Duff is an icon!

26:48.753 --> 26:50.651
Yeah, but some folks
prefer Pawtucket Pat.

26:50.686 --> 26:53.850
I mean, don't get me wrong,
I-I used to love Duff when I was younger,

26:53.885 --> 26:56.750
but I-I haven't even had it
in, like, 13 years.

26:56.785 --> 26:58.017
Be that as it may,

26:58.052 --> 27:00.616
I represent the Duff Brewery,
and you, sir,

27:00.652 --> 27:02.949
as a representative
of Pawtucket Patriot Ale,

27:02.984 --> 27:06.581
are being sued for intellectual
theft and patent infringement.

27:06.616 --> 27:08.415
Aha! Intellectual theft!

27:08.449 --> 27:10.648
What do you have to say
about that, Griffin?

27:10.683 --> 27:12.014
D'oh!

27:24.704 --> 27:27.401
The Pawtucket Patriot
Brewery being sued?

27:27.437 --> 27:29.934
It's the largest employer
in Quahog, Peter.

27:29.970 --> 27:32.267
A lot of people's jobs
are riding on this.

27:32.302 --> 27:34.601
Yeah, I got a job for you
riding on something.

27:34.636 --> 27:35.667
Peter!

27:35.703 --> 27:37.267
Sorry! Sorry, Lois,
I'm-I'm tired

27:37.302 --> 27:40.299
'cause we usually only do
these things for half an hour.

27:42.468 --> 27:43.499
Simpson.

27:43.535 --> 27:44.533
Griffin.

27:44.534 --> 27:45.699
Nice day, isn't it?

27:45.734 --> 27:47.498
A nice day for stabbing
a friend in the back.

27:47.534 --> 27:51.065
Yeah, and a nice day for
bringing thieves to justice.

27:52.199 --> 27:53.965
We're getting a
lot of compliments.

27:54.000 --> 27:56.464
Yep, we're doing
something right.

27:59.032 --> 28:01.463
Your Honor,
citizens of Springfield

28:01.498 --> 28:04.196
and visitors from Quahog,
my client, the Duff Brewery,

28:04.232 --> 28:07.295
is the victim of flagrant
intellectual theft.

28:07.331 --> 28:09.962
I'm whispering in court
to look smart.

28:09.997 --> 28:13.294
But it's not just the main Duff
recipe that's been plagiarized.

28:13.330 --> 28:15.794
Several other Duff variations,
packages

28:15.829 --> 28:18.393
and design elements
have been similarly infringed,

28:18.429 --> 28:20.293
resulting again

28:20.329 --> 28:22.227
and again in pale imitations,

28:22.262 --> 28:23.426
chp coes,
clumsy counterfeits

28:23.461 --> 28:26.658
and weak substitutions.

28:26.694 --> 28:28.325
You like sex?
Eh.

28:28.360 --> 28:30.059
I don't think
we're very similar.

28:30.094 --> 28:32.857
You know why they got us
sitting next to each other.

28:32.893 --> 28:35.524
Uh, 'cause we're the two
funniest guys in our towns?

28:35.559 --> 28:36.990
Damn right.

28:37.025 --> 28:38.490
I'm a Jewish clown.

28:38.525 --> 28:39.890
Me, too.

28:39.925 --> 28:42.056
Are you a mayor?
Yes, I am.

28:42.091 --> 28:44.056
Are you a "cool" mayor?

28:44.091 --> 28:46.622
I, uh... I like
to think so.

28:49.656 --> 28:50.955
You lived in Springfield?

28:50.990 --> 28:53.821
Yeah, I worked at the
Kwik-E-Mart, researching a role.

28:53.856 --> 28:56.087
These guys are gonna lose.

28:56.122 --> 28:59.687
I've heard all I need to
hear to make a decision.

28:59.722 --> 29:03.286
If you ask me, neither of
these beers is wholly original.

29:03.322 --> 29:07.219
They're both pale imitations
of my favorite beer, Bud Rock.

29:07.254 --> 29:08.519
- Oh, ho, ho!
- Ooh!

29:08.554 --> 29:10.985
But rendering a verdict
is something

29:11.020 --> 29:14.251
I'm paid to yabba-dabba-do!

29:14.286 --> 29:15.584
Eh.

29:15.619 --> 29:18.183
And I find in favor of Duff.

29:18.219 --> 29:19.083
Oh, no!

29:19.118 --> 29:19.916
Oh, no!

29:19.952 --> 29:21.283
Oh, no!

29:24.785 --> 29:25.915
Hello?

29:25.951 --> 29:27.015
Uh, hey.

29:27.051 --> 29:29.249
I'm-I'm
in the wrong Springfield.

29:33.950 --> 29:35.846
So what's going
to happen now?

29:35.882 --> 29:38.314
Well, the Pawtucket Brewery
will be shut down,

29:38.349 --> 29:42.214
so I guess we got to go back to
Quahog and find Peter a new job.

29:42.248 --> 29:43.812
Mmm, that's too bad.

29:43.847 --> 29:47.146
Yeah. Anyways, it was still nice
to meet you and your family,

29:47.181 --> 29:49.478
even though you kind of
screwed us over.

29:49.514 --> 29:50.945
Good to have you.

29:50.980 --> 29:53.111
And, hey, next time
you stay with a family,

29:53.147 --> 29:56.277
maybe you can wear a
bra some of the time.

29:56.313 --> 29:59.210
Hey, uh, Marge, uh,

29:59.245 --> 30:01.483
listen, there's something
difficult that I've been trying

30:01.512 --> 30:03.976
to figure out how to
tell you, and, um...

30:04.011 --> 30:06.841
it's about, uh,
Santa's Little Helper.

30:06.877 --> 30:08.075
What about him?

30:08.110 --> 30:09.808
He's, um...

30:11.909 --> 30:13.840
...right there.

30:13.876 --> 30:16.507
You were trying to figure out
a way to tell me that?

30:16.542 --> 30:18.307
I overthink things
sometimes.

30:18.342 --> 30:20.640
Oh, and, look,
he's with Ed McMahon!

30:20.676 --> 30:22.339
Hey-o!

30:22.374 --> 30:23.839
Here's Johnny!

30:23.875 --> 30:25.172
Chris, we're done.

30:25.208 --> 30:28.172
You may be, but...
"I'm just getting warmed up!"

30:28.208 --> 30:30.705
That's Al Pacino.

30:30.740 --> 30:32.637
Thanks for being
so cool, Lisa.

30:32.673 --> 30:35.270
I cut your name in my arm
so I'll always remember you.

30:38.639 --> 30:40.770
Meg, I want you to have this.

30:40.805 --> 30:42.070
Your saxophone?

30:42.104 --> 30:46.373
Yes, Meg.
When you played the saxophone,

30:49.241 --> 30:53.204
Lisa, no one has ever done
anything this nice for me.

30:53.240 --> 30:56.605
You're amazing,
and I will never be like you.

30:56.640 --> 30:59.737
I'm not pretty, I'm not smart,
I'm not talented.

30:59.773 --> 31:02.004
I have the same shoe size
as Charles Barkley.

31:02.038 --> 31:03.870
My prom date
was a scarecrow I stole,

31:03.905 --> 31:05.603
and he left
with someone else.

31:05.638 --> 31:08.136
The inside of my hat
smells so bad I'm not allowed

31:08.171 --> 31:10.369
in most restaurants...
Hey, hey!

31:10.404 --> 31:12.368
Shut up, Meg.

31:19.603 --> 31:22.067
No luggage. Car's full.
Let's go.

31:23.069 --> 31:24.700
Well, nice knowing you,
Stewie.

31:24.735 --> 31:26.166
Same here, Bart.

31:26.201 --> 31:27.666
Hey, I hope
you don't mind,

31:27.702 --> 31:29.665
I got you a
little present.

31:32.401 --> 31:34.364
Whoa. Is that Nelson?

31:34.400 --> 31:36.164
Stewie, what the deuce?

31:36.199 --> 31:38.164
Yes, I... Oh!
Oh, that's nice.

31:38.199 --> 31:40.097
You got that from me.
'Cause, you know,

31:40.133 --> 31:42.296
I was starting to worry
this was a one-way thing.

31:42.332 --> 31:44.029
You kidnapped him?

31:44.065 --> 31:45.996
I kidnapped all your enemies.

31:46.031 --> 31:49.462
Nelson, Jimbo, Principal
Skinner, Sideshow Bob, Apu.

31:49.498 --> 31:52.261
I know Apu's not your enemy,
but I just wanted to say,

31:52.296 --> 31:54.695
"I took Apu."

31:54.730 --> 31:57.094
That is funny!

31:57.130 --> 31:58.961
But the rest of this?
It's messed up, man.

31:58.996 --> 32:00.594
I know! Isn't it awesome?

32:00.629 --> 32:02.960
So, how do you want to keep
in touch? Facebook? Twitter?

32:02.995 --> 32:04.726
Late-night phone calls
lying on our tummies

32:04.762 --> 32:06.193
with our feet up in the air?

32:06.229 --> 32:07.725
Stewie, I don't think
we can be friends.

32:07.761 --> 32:09.326
You freak me out.

32:09.361 --> 32:11.859
Bart, if we don't keep in touch,
I'll kill myself.

32:11.894 --> 32:13.191
That's what I'm talking about.

32:13.227 --> 32:15.125
Later, dude!

32:15.160 --> 32:16.991
Later...

32:17.026 --> 32:18.758
dude.

32:19.793 --> 32:22.424
Haw-haw!

32:48.059 --> 32:49.790
Aw.

32:51.191 --> 32:52.490
Hey, Griffin.

32:52.525 --> 32:54.656
Sorry about your job.

32:54.691 --> 32:56.588
I was just sticking
up for Duff.

32:56.623 --> 32:57.756
I love Duff.

32:57.791 --> 32:59.288
And Duff loves me.

32:59.323 --> 33:00.721
Duff can keep a secret.

33:00.757 --> 33:02.187
Duff never says no.

33:02.223 --> 33:05.288
Duff is more experimental than
any partner I've ever had.

33:05.323 --> 33:08.654
Anyway, the point
is, I'm sorry.

33:08.689 --> 33:11.920
You know, when I first met you,
I thought, hey, I love this guy!

33:11.955 --> 33:13.686
This is the funniest guy
I've ever met.

33:13.721 --> 33:15.686
I'm gonna quote this guy
to all my friends.

33:15.721 --> 33:17.718
I love his town,
I love his family.

33:17.754 --> 33:20.285
But now, I think
I speak for all of us

33:20.320 --> 33:23.184
when I say,
I am over the Simpsons!

33:23.220 --> 33:25.217
Wh-What
are you saying?

33:25.252 --> 33:27.317
I'm saying
the Simpsons suck!

33:27.352 --> 33:29.050
Why, you...

33:56.948 --> 33:59.379
Ow! What the hell?
That really hurts.

33:59.414 --> 34:02.711
No, it doesn't!
I do it to my son all the time.

34:02.747 --> 34:04.645
You strangle your son?
That's insane!

34:04.680 --> 34:07.810
No wonder he's fat and stupid
and masturbates all the time.

34:07.846 --> 34:09.043
<i>That's your son!</i>

34:40.741 --> 34:42.271
Phew!

34:49.272 --> 34:51.936
Hey! Knock it off!
There's a kid back there!

34:51.971 --> 34:54.502
I'm in danger.

35:34.164 --> 35:37.629
Hey, that's no fair.
I don't got none of them.

35:45.030 --> 35:46.627
Uh-oh.

35:53.128 --> 35:55.093
Hey, hey!

35:55.128 --> 35:56.325
Uh-oh.

36:13.459 --> 36:14.756
Ooh.

36:51.952 --> 36:53.316
Damn it!

36:57.384 --> 37:00.249
And remember, kids,
TV violence is fine

37:00.284 --> 37:02.648
as long as you
don't show a nipple.

37:20.480 --> 37:21.744
Perfect.

37:21.779 --> 37:24.611
The earthlings are
destroying themselves.

37:24.646 --> 37:27.077
Yeah, it's really great,
isn't it, guys?

37:27.112 --> 37:29.077
We went to summer camp together.

37:34.512 --> 37:36.876
Bye! Thanks for having me.

37:39.244 --> 37:40.876
Huh?

37:44.409 --> 37:46.741
It appears that I
am now the only one

37:46.776 --> 37:48.508
with radioactive powers,

37:48.543 --> 37:51.140
which will allow me
to unleash my fury...

37:51.176 --> 37:53.373
Oh, I talked too long.

38:24.003 --> 38:26.267
<i>- We're gonna make it!
- Trust me, we're not.</i>

38:40.300 --> 38:41.598
Huh?
Huh?

38:41.633 --> 38:43.098
Huh?
Huh? Huh?

38:49.099 --> 38:50.231
Whoa!

38:50.266 --> 38:51.396
Whoo-hoo!

38:52.332 --> 38:53.463
Road house.

39:12.495 --> 39:14.193
Aah-aah!

40:13.085 --> 40:15.983
Say hi to Maude Flanders.

40:17.151 --> 40:20.549
<i>No. You say hi
to Muriel Goldman.</i>

40:20.585 --> 40:21.082
Who?

40:51.879 --> 40:54.076
What are you
still doing here?

40:54.111 --> 40:56.009
I think you're gonna get
a kick out of this.

40:56.045 --> 40:57.942
You're parked behind me
at your place.

40:57.977 --> 40:59.076
<i>That is funny.</i>

40:59.111 --> 41:00.409
Hey, listen, I...

41:00.444 --> 41:02.175
I'm sorry we fought.

41:02.211 --> 41:04.808
I just wanted
to make you laugh and cry.

41:04.844 --> 41:07.007
<i>You see, I'm a Family Guy.</i>

41:07.043 --> 41:08.107
I understand.

41:08.143 --> 41:10.340
<i>I'm a The Simpsons.</i>

41:10.375 --> 41:12.973
Look, even if we
don't work as best pals,

41:13.008 --> 41:15.207
I respect you.
You, too.

41:15.242 --> 41:18.638
Let's just agree to stay a half hour
away from each other.

41:18.674 --> 41:21.405
With a pile of
garbage between us.

41:22.907 --> 41:26.404
Worst chicken fight ever.

41:30.372 --> 41:32.696
It sure is nice to
be back in Quahog.

41:32.697 --> 41:36.161
Oh, and thank God all the commotion
about Dad's comic blew over.

41:36.196 --> 41:38.527
Oh, my God, I had a comic?
That's hilarious!

41:38.562 --> 41:40.727
Well, you may not be
a cartoonist anymore,

41:40.763 --> 41:43.427
but you are a local hero
for defending our beer,

41:43.462 --> 41:46.526
and apparently, that's more
important than hating women.

41:46.561 --> 41:49.425
So here you go,
a Pawtucket Patriot Ale.

41:49.460 --> 41:52.058
What? I don't understand.
Ain't the brewery out of business?

41:52.093 --> 41:54.091
We lost a court case.
Yes, we lost,

41:54.127 --> 41:55.858
but how are they
gonna enforce it?

41:55.893 --> 41:57.658
<i>What, are they
gonna come here?</i>

41:57.693 --> 42:00.090
I think we know that's
never gonna happen.

42:00.126 --> 42:02.790
Hey, Stewie, I'm sorry Bart
didn't want to be your friend.

42:02.825 --> 42:04.657
What? No! What are
you talking about?

42:04.692 --> 42:06.423
He was lame.
If you ask me,

42:06.458 --> 42:08.590
he kind of sounded like a girl.
Really?

42:08.625 --> 42:10.322
Kind of seemed like
you idolized him.

42:10.357 --> 42:13.188
And I can understand losing
a friend and feeling rejected.

42:13.224 --> 42:14.721
Course you can!
You're a loser.

42:14.757 --> 42:16.488
But not me.
I'm a lone wolf.

42:16.523 --> 42:19.054
Speaking of which,
I'm gonna go howl at the moon.

42:19.089 --> 42:21.254
Don't need nobody.

42:49.852 --> 42:51.082
Shh.

42:51.118 --> 42:54.382
♪ And now the show
is over now. ♪

42:54.383 --> 43:55.312
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru